_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":44,"quote":"Additionally, Cvetkov-Iliev et al. [70] model table as a knowledge graph, where the feature values or rows represent nodes, and the column names represent the relations."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_137eb5cc86a77feb","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":21,"quote":"NER and OpenIE are sequentially conducted on each passage of the corpus. Thus, an open knowledge graph is formed for the entire corpus."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_63b70d30e6c602f7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"On the Knowledge Graph (KG), retrieval granularity includes Entity, Triplet, and sub-Graph."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_c5f3ca0d35888835","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":18,"quote":"It can either encompass a broad spectrum of general knowledge, such as the widely recognized Google Knowledge Graph [53, 261], or delve deeply into specialized domains, like the BioASQ dataset [400] for biomedical reasoning."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_d441d2311abddb2e","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":12,"quote":"For instance, if the retrieved subgraph is a path within a knowledge graph, we can aggregate the embeddings of the nodes and relations along that path to form a cohesive path embedding.2 Eventually, the resulting embeddings for different"},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_78b95e7ba2cf113d","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":53,"quote":"By reviewing GraphRAG applications across varied domains—from knowledge graphs and document graphs to scientific and social graphs, we illustrated how its flexibility allows it to meet unique demands and add"},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_ae1a85080b0608ff","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":3,"quote":"• Specialization of GraphRAG in different domains: We categorize GraphRAG designs into 10 distinct domains based on their specific applications, including knowledge graph , document graph , scientific graph , social graph , planning &"},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_17e8bcc3c9b25731","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":49,"quote":"49 10.2 Retriever • Differentiating Neural and Symbolic Knowledge: Graph-structured data usually involves two distinct types of knowledge: symbolic-formatted knowledge, such as relations in knowledge graphs, and neural-formatted knowledge,"},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_988bcdc059305602","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":4,"quote":"• Self Canonicalization: Absent a target schema, the goal is to consolidate semanti- cally similar schema components, standardiz- ing them to a singular representation to stream- line the KG."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_e7bd98d8333ef3fb","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":8,"quote":"A survey on knowledge graphs: Representation, acquisition, and applications."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_fe2db08674d547ef","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":5,"quote":"3.1.4 Knowledge Graph →Graph Communities Given the graph index created in the previous step, a variety of community detection algorithms may be used to partition the graph into communities of strongly connected nodes (e.g., see the surveys"},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_05db18140b2a4a5d","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":3,"quote":"Coreference resolution identifies and connects different references of the same entity, keeping coherence within the knowledge graph."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_565b7707a80ea104","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"LLM-based KGC methods employ various innovative prompt-based techniques, such as multi-turn conversation (Wei et al., 2023) and code generation (Bi et al., 2024), to generate entity- relation triplets that represent the knowledge graph."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_fc13e30f668eafd2","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":8,"quote":"Knowledge graphs in finance: Applications and opportunities."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_07fff3f6c0245670","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":68,"quote":"Explore then determine: A gnn-llm synergy framework for reasoning over knowledge graph."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_238eddf1321770b1","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":2,"quote":"2.2 Knowledge Graph Construction A KG is a structured representation of real-world entities, their attributes, and their relations, usually stored in a graph database or a triplet store, i.e., a KG consists of nodes that represent entities"},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_755ad0b51856cc19","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":1,"quote":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction Bhaskarjit Sarmah bhaskarjit.sarmah@blackrock.com BlackRock, Inc."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_208c9f049fdd3c81","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":2,"quote":"In most methodologies to build a KG from given documents, three main steps are involved: knowledge extraction, knowledge 1https://www.nseindia.com/products/content/equities/indices/nifty_50.htm HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and"},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_5e589a49f40ba753","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":5,"quote":"In the final step of the knowledge graph extraction process, these instances of entities and rela- tionships become individual nodes and edges in the graph."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_be9a60a662d79ce8","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":16,"quote":"Representation learning of large-scale knowledge graphs via entity feature combinations."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_1aac7ff9f2103b41","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":29,"quote":"What medication should I take for it?\" In graghRAG, the scientific literature is usually converted into a knowledge graph to provide a basis for answering questions or to enrich the query."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_e32318e66b415c47","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":3,"quote":"A subgraph, which consists of these relevant nodes and edges, is extracted from the full KG to provide context."},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_36f42e6c927e3d4a","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":10,"quote":"A survey on knowledge graphs: Representation, acquisition, and applications."},{"id":"c39","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_60f78cb541da571c","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":9,"quote":"Specifically, KGs can form memory sources for VLMs, containing facts about humans (Zhang and Soh, 2023), the task or goal (Xie et al., 2023), and the environment."},{"id":"c40","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_8ecf3c454742d1ca","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":4,"quote":"After the LLM makes its choice, the relations are transformed to yield: [‘Alan Shepard’, ‘birthDate’, ‘Nov 18, 1923’], [‘Alan Shepard’, ‘mission’, ‘Apollo 14’], which forms our canonicalized KG."},{"id":"c41","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_988bcdc059305602","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":4,"quote":"Starting with an empty canonical schema, we examine the open KG triplets, searching for potential consolidation candi- dates through vector similarity and LLM veri- fication."},{"id":"c42","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_ba3f7247d56ece0e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"1 Introduction Knowledge graphs (KGs) (Ji et al., 2021) are a structured representation of knowledge that orga- nizes interconnected information through graph structures, where entities and relations are rep- resented as nodes and edges."},{"id":"c43","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_cc8c385b6ddbc31f","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"Furthermore, there are scenar- ios where a fixed pre-defined schema is not available and we would like the method to con- struct a high-quality KG with a succinct self- generated schema."},{"id":"c44","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_efc29b64e87e985f","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":8,"quote":"Following prior work (Wadhwa et al., 2023; Kolluru et al., 2020), we conducted a tar- geted human evaluation of knowledge graphs."},{"id":"c45","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_784801446a75a137","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":1,"quote":"HippoRAG synergistically orchestrates LLMs, knowledge graphs, and the Personalized PageRank algorithm to mimic the different roles of neocortex and hippocampus in human memory."},{"id":"c46","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_347747745d362e3f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":2,"quote":"For example, document graphs embed entities as sentence chunks [98, 428], knowledge graphs store graph information as triplets or paths [38], and molecule graphs consist of higher-order structures (e.g., cellular complexes) [26], as shown"},{"id":"c47","chunkId":"bd72eebf611df136_c_88b7bb092e53e118","docId":"bd72eebf611df136","docTitle":"2410.05779_LightRAG_Simple_and_Fast_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"We formally represent this graph generation module as follows: ˆD = (ˆV, ˆE) = Dedupe ◦Prof(V, E), V, E = ∪Di∈DRecog(Di) (2) where ˆD represents the resulting knowledge graphs."},{"id":"c48","chunkId":"d2